  "id": "tigrinya_music_eritrean",
  "name": "Tigrinya music (Eritrean / northern Ethiopian)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Tigrinya vocal-and-string tradition of Eritrea and the Tigray region of northern Ethiopia, sharing the qenet pentatonic mode-system with broader Habesha practice but with Tigrinya-language poetic-meter and Eritrean-highland melodic-contour conventions. Performance ranges from solo wata one-string spike-fiddle to ensembles with krar bowl-lyre, masenqo, kebero drum, and washint flute. Distinguished from Amhara azmari by Tigrinya-language repertoire and Asmara-Mendefera-Massawa dialect.",
